# See https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# compiled output
dist
tmp
out-tsc
*.tsbuildinfo
.expo
.expo-shared

# dependencies
node_modules

# IDEs and editors
/.idea
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace

# IDE - VSCode
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# misc
/.sass-cache
/connect.lock
/coverage
**/coverage/
/libpeerconnection.log
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
testem.log
/typings

# System Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.cursor/rules/nx-rules.mdc
.github/instructions/nx.instructions.md

# Replit
.cache/
.local/*
!.local/tasks/
!.local/tasks/**
attached_assets/
# npm-global installs in the Repl (e.g. Claude Code via `npm install -g`)
# land under the workspace's .config so they persist across restarts —
# tool binaries, not project files; keep them out of checkpoint commits.
.config/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (per-session ephemeral)
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code personal/local settings (machine-specific, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code user config dir for the in-Repl install (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR in
# .replit). Holds OAuth credentials + session history. It lives inside the
# workspace only because that's what persists across Repl restarts — it must
# NEVER be committed: this repo is public, and Replit Agent auto-commits the
# workspace at checkpoints, so an untracked credentials dir WILL eventually be
# swept into a pushed commit without this entry.
.claude-user/

# Secrets — never commit env files (allow *.example templates)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Database dumps / backups — NEVER commit. NOTE: real Drizzle migrations live in
# lib/db/migrations/*.sql and MUST stay tracked, so these patterns are narrow —
# do NOT replace them with a blanket *.sql (that would hide 87 real migrations).
/prod-backup-*.sql
/backups/
*.dump

# Derived copy of artifacts/api-server/src/assets/ — build.mjs (and a dev-stack
# boot) materializes it next to dist/ so the bundled server can resolve
# ../assets. The canonical, tracked sources live under src/assets/.
artifacts/api-server/assets/

# Receipts split by KIND, and the line is evidence vs. decision.
#
# EVIDENCE is session-local, not repo history: each file describes one PR at
# one moment, is worthless once the moment passes, and is re-derivable at will.
# Both shapes below are ignored --
#   pr-*.json               readiness, quoted in a merge claim and checked by the merge hook
#   loop-round-check-*.json rounds counted from a snapshot for the budget guard
#
# DECISIONS (loop-budget-*.json, loop-extension-*.json) are committed instead.
# They are taken once and bind afterwards, and they MUST survive the container
# or tripwire 2 can never fire: an ephemeral extension record means a loop that
# already spent its one self-serve adjudication is offered the self-serve
# tripwire again by the next session, forever.
#
# Named shapes rather than `.agents/receipts/` + negations, because git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded -- the negations read
# correctly and do nothing. The cost is that a NEW evidence shape must be added
# here; the benefit is that the rule actually works. A new file in this
# directory that is evidence belongs on this list.
#
# The round COUNT is deliberately evidence. It was a committed file in this
# mechanism's first design, and that is precisely what failed: a cache of state
# GitHub already holds, which drifted from it four different ways in one
# evening.
.agents/receipts/pr-*.json
.agents/receipts/loop-round-check-*.json
